<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/doc-template/templates/page">
<$fill $name="body">

!! The single hook point

Streams renders every node's content through one template, `$:/plugins/sq/streams/templates/stream-row-body`, whose entire body is:

```
<$transclude mode="block"/>
```

That renders the node tiddler's own body in block mode. It does //not// pass through `$:/core/ui/ViewTemplate`, which is why kind's ViewTemplate-attached field bar never shows up inside a Streams outline.

kind-streams ships its own copy of that template. The copy gates on a cheap `has[kind.type]` test and, for typed nodes only, transcludes the node bar //above// the body:

```
<%if [<currentTiddler>has[kind.type]] :filter[…enable…] %><$transclude $tiddler="…/node-bar"/><%endif%>
<$transclude mode="block"/>
```

!! Winning the shadow

Two plugins now define `stream-row-body`. TiddlyWiki assigns shadows by ascending `plugin-priority` (default 1), so the last writer wins. Streams is priority 1; kind-streams declares `plugin-priority: 2`, so its copy deterministically overrides. (A tie would break alphabetically — `rimir…` sorts before `sq…` and would //lose// — hence the explicit `2`.)

!! Lazy rendering

`node-bar` renders a cheap pill by default. The expensive field bar lives inside `<$reveal type="match" text="open">`, whose children are not rendered until the state tiddler `$:/state/rimir/kind-streams/open/<node>` equals `open`. So the per-field iteration only runs for nodes the user expands.

!! Reuse, not reimplementation

* Expanded bar → transcludes kind's `stream-view` (needs `target-tid` in scope).
* Assign submenu → reuses kind's type filter (`kind.top-level-types` + `kind.belongs-to-ns`), rendered with Streams' own `sq-contextmenu` markup so it matches the parent menu.

Neither piece is duplicated here; this plugin only supplies the wiring, the lazy wrapper, and the CSS.

!! Two overrides

kind-streams overrides two Streams templates (both by `plugin-priority: 2`):

* `stream-row-body` — injects the node bar above the node content (typed nodes only).
* `contextmenu/contextmenu-template` — a faithful copy of the upstream menu with one added ''Kind type ▸'' flyout item (`contextmenu-kind-submenu`), using `tc-popup-keep` so the parent menu stays open. If a future Streams release changes either template, re-sync the copy.

</$fill>
</$transclude>
